Licensed under Apache-2.0; see LICENSE. HYLE adaptations isolate the
namespace and support macro and omit unrelated host glue. The original
activation arithmetic and packed indexing are retained.

C1-AB additionally extracts the pinned RMSNorm warp/CTA/double-load bodies
and norm/tile helpers, retaining their algorithm and reduction order. Host
binding and primitive CUDA shims replace TVM/Python glue; the Blackwell-only
32-byte path is not included. The Unary kernel shell uses an explicitly
adapted stable-tail formula and -infinity limiting value for HYLE's ordinary
Unary contract. Unary input/output restrict qualifiers are removed to permit
the documented exact in-place alias. See provenance.json for source hashes.

D5-F37 additionally retains the unchanged group128 quantizer and block128
FP8 GEMM Python source bodies for offline AOT. Only the original GEMM's
SM89 cubin is embedded in the native HYLE Provider. Triton 3.8.0 generated
the artifact; its MIT notice is retained in TRITON-LICENSE. Normal builds
and native use do not run Python, Triton or a model engine. See fp8/ for
compiler/source identities and explicit maintainer regeneration.

D5-F38 adds the original BF16 quantizer variants and BF16 GEMM output.
The power-of-two quantizer retains its original column-major F32 scales;
HYLE passes the matching GEMM strides. The absmax floor remains the original
runtime argument and is explicitly part of the model operation contract.

The F38 finite correction replaces ordinary-scale quantization with unchanged
SGLang CUDA GroupReduceMax/per_token_group_quant_8bit_kernel bodies. Their
CUDA FP8 constructor avoids Triton's SM89 intermediate F16 truncation.
FlashInfer vec_dtypes.cuh at 69ff11fc4954396d98326656dc85debd2223f637 supplies
the original vector loads during offline compilation; its Apache-2.0 notice
is in FLASHINFER-LICENSE. The inline attribute is expressed with CUDA
__forceinline__ for MSVC; vector bodies are unchanged. The two superseded
ordinary Triton cubins are removed from the current product. Pow2/GEMM
artifacts retain their qualified identities. See fp8/cuda-quant-compilation.json.

D5-F39 adds the original grouped FP8 GEMM bodies and the original CUDA
small/generic expert alignment programs. The alignment adapter checks all
expert IDs before expert-indexed memory access and reports the existing
device error code; valid sorting/scan/GEMM arithmetic is unchanged. Four
offline GEMM variants and one checked alignment cubin are embedded. The
original default tile and host small/generic selection are retained; no
per-expert host loop, runtime JIT or search is added. See fp8/grouped/ for
source identities, launch ABI records and maintainer-only regeneration.
